      "message": "Some time ago I proposed change doing same thing, but one layer above:\ngo/aog/2282794\n\nBut then we had some discussions with Rahul and noticed that BTGATT_MAX_ATTR_LEN was not updated when GATT_MAX_ATTR_LEN was lowered to 512.\n\nSo maybe also lower the BTGATT_MAX_ATTR_LEN to 512 ? It would trim the values coming from Java, instead of returning error code.\n\n\nI actually like returning error code more than trimming the value, but you should also update comment on https://developer.android.com/reference/android/bluetooth/BluetoothGatt#writeCharacteristic(android.bluetooth.BluetoothGattCharacteristic,%20byte[],%20int)\n\nAnd define error code returned to Java, as now it\u0027s not specified what 0x0d means in java, and in \"Returns\" section.\n\n\nShould same be done for write descriptor ?",
